  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A sequence of numbers is called an **arithmetic progression** if the difference between any two consecutive elements is the same.\n\nWith an array of numbers `arr`, output `true` *if the array can be rearranged to form an **arithmetic progression**. Otherwise, output* `false`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: arr = [3,5,1]\nOutput: true\nExplanation: We can reorder the elements as [1,3,5] or [5,3,1] with differences 2 and -2 respectively, between each consecutive elements.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: arr = [1,2,4]\nOutput: false\nExplanation: There is no way to reorder the elements to obtain an arithmetic progression.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `2 <= arr.length <= 1000`\n* `-106 <= arr[i] <= 106`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
